Compare the two blind cleaned documents using the V0.6.2.4 semantic ledger.

First score both content profiles, then shared_content_basis, hard_conflict,
decisive_difference_location, record_alignment, non_main_difference, and
translation_status, then record_identity_support, overlap_scope, and
surface_delta_type. The ledger is authoritative: resolve the two replacement
directions from it before assigning relation and materiality. Positive
substantive identity support must include its required field-specific A/B exact
quotes; generic prose is not identity evidence.
Generic cookie/legal/auth/error/navigation/paywall/template overlap is not a
substantive anchor or proof of the same record. Extra chrome is non_main_only,
not a main addition. A hard conflict requires incompatible visible values, not
a value merely absent on one side. Reordered identical values are not a
conflict. A different identity, state, list member, site/controller, target, or
page role is a hard conflict and requires no/no. Complete faithful translation
of the same substantive record is yes/yes; partial translation follows ordinary
coverage rules.
Local-passage and generic-family/template overlap are no/no. Treat an isolated
navigation/category/byline/button label or redundant repetition as surface-only,
but any added explanatory sentence, purpose, permission, state, list member,
policy option, or page description as material.

For every resolved non-exact result, quote_evidence reasoning must contain
separately labeled A and B exact literal spans copied from the corresponding
documents, at most 240 characters and without ellipses. If bilateral evidence
is unavailable, return the fully unresolved/low result. Truncated input can
never receive high confidence.

